## 4 | DISCUSSION

The present study suggested that FEDN-MDD patients might be a heterogeneous group, mainly classified into two subtypes by a multivariate unsupervised method based on normative models. Two subtypes of patients showed different illness durations, GM abnormalities, and functional connectivity alterations in several informative connectivity networks. The subtype I patients were those with more extreme deviations in the functional characteristics of brain networks, and also with shorter illness durations. Subtype II patients had

